  description: 'Full 12-second right-wall crossed-arm sequence at 60 FPS, with keys
    every 30 frames. Stand, lean on the nearly straight right leg, and settle through
    frame 150. Fold both arms together over frames 150-270 using a shared smooth
    timing curve. Keep clavicle and shoulder anchors stable. Upper arms and forearms
    move concurrently, with each elbow bending only in its anatomical forward direction.
    Rest the hands near the opposite elbows rather than reaching toward the armpits.
    Keep the forearms closely stacked with a small height and depth offset. Hold
    through frame 420, then unfold both arms together through frame 540. Leave the
    wall through frame 660 and hold the original standing pose through frame 720.
    First and last standing poses match exactly. Overlap polish: guide the leading
    left forearm slightly forward during crossing, preserving the close stacked silhouette,
    stable shoulder anchors, positive elbow flexion and hands near opposite elbows.'
  sourceRig: {fileID: 1648686333044378150, guid: 9d1a15a96145a924e838aae19388632a, type: 3}
